# M6 red team: reply capabilities and bound notifications attacked from
# ring 3 (user/root/src/redteam/ipc.rs); they held. A server
# saves a client's reply capability with CNode_SaveCaller; suspending and
# resuming the client must delete it, so a Send on it reaches nobody, and a
# saved reply sent twice reaches the client once. A thread bound to a
# notification is deleted while it waits on an endpoint: the notification
# must be unbound, pollable and bindable again, and deleting a notification
# whose bound thread waits on an endpoint leaves that thread queued.
cmdline: test=redteam-ipc
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: root: cmdline "test=redteam-ipc"
expect: redteam: ipc: S saved C's reply capability into slot
expect: redteam: ipc: suspend and resume of C deleted the saved reply capability; a Send on X reached nobody
expect: redteam: ipc: two Sends on a saved reply capability: C got the first (0x600d) and only it
expect: redteam: ipc: B, bound to N and waiting on E3, woke with N's badge; N and B cannot be bound twice
expect: redteam: ipc: B's deletion unbound N; N was Active for a poll, then bound to B2, which its signal woke
expect: redteam: ipc: deleting N left B2 queued on E3, unbound: E3's message reached it, and it bound to N2
expect: redteam: ipc: every reply and binding attack held
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
